include g474.tdc
diagram esw-slow "ISR → thread with USE_SWITCH=y, slow mode (80 %): one SysTick reprogram, then the switch at the end of the ISR"
letter "E-sw slow"
new
num value "1829 cycles"
num share "79.8 %"
num path "wrapped ISR, k_sem, defaults"
num arch "USE_SWITCH=y (no PendSV)"
what "The same path as card E-sw fast, with one more step: the new slice timeout is the first timeout, so the driver programs SysTick again inside the ISR. Then the switch runs at the ISR exit. The dashed cursor shows where the fast mode ends (card E-sw fast)."
evidence "Mode distance 309 cycles: one reprogram, as with PendSV (313). The run of 2026-10-25 gave 301 (ws-safety) and 328 (ws-up); the study now has only the tree ws-up."
evidence "USE_SWITCH=y costs about 250 cycles more per wake than PendSV in this mode (1829 against 1582)."
evidence "The slice reset and the reprogram are in update_cache(), before the arch switch. So the arch interface does not change them."
src "wake-anchors-1m/20261029T014607Z"

axis "cycles after the edge" -100..2000

idle sleep -100..4 "WFI"
mask -100..9 "PRIMASK"
mask 150..1156 "BASEPRI" : The give, the slice reset and the reprogram run with the scheduler lock and the timeout lock held (card E fast).
mask 1161..1839 "BASEPRI until the switch ends" : arm_m_must_switch() sets BASEPRI (arch/arm/core/cortex_m/arm-m-switch.c:518). arm_m_exc_exit releases it at the end of the context switch (:639).
at 0
hw 60 "entry" : Pin, EXTI, NVIC, wake-up, exception entry, _isr_wrapper. Cold cache.
dev 21 : The ISR reads TIM2->CNT: time stamp 1.
dev 250 "give" : k_sem_give(): the waiting thread becomes ready, and update_cache() selects it.
dev 516? "slice reset" : The same slice reset as in the fast mode (card E-sw fast).
dev 309! "reprogram" : The new slice timeout is the first timeout, so the driver programs SysTick again. 309 cycles: the distance of the two modes, measured.
dev 683 "exc exit: pick thread, switch" : arm_m_exc_exit, arm_m_must_switch(), z_get_next_switch_handle(), arm_m_do_switch(), in handler mode. No PendSV, and no second slice reset.
hw 15 : Exception return directly into the woken thread.
waker 56 : The thread returns from k_sem_take() and reads TIM2->CNT: time stamp 2.

@t0_1 edge "edge" at 0
@t0_2 stamp "stamp 1" at 81
@t0_3 ref "fast mode" at 1601
@t0_4 stamp "stamp 2" at 1910
span 0..81 "81" !
span 81..1910 "1829, measured" !
span 847..1156 "309" !
